SDE WM: no input method server for the window manager.

Openbox opens the X input method of XMODIFIERS (IBus, Fcitx) for its key
bindings, menus and prompts. XIM calls wait for the server's answer without
a timeout. When IBus restarted (ibus restart, or its panel or XIM server
crashing), the keymap change that followed made obt_keyboard_reload() call
XDestroyIC() on the input context of the server that was gone, and it
waited forever in _XimRead(): no window was mapped, moved or focused any
more, the restarted SDE panel stayed unmapped, and the desktop looked frozen
until the machine was switched off. Reproduced on Xvfb with ibus-daemon and
its GTK panel; the backtrace was XIfEvent < _XimRead < XDestroyIC <
obt_keyboard_shutdown < obt_keyboard_reload.

The window manager only uses the local input method (Compose sequences) now
(XSetLocaleModifiers("@im=none")), as the SDE panel does. XSetLocaleModifiers
does not change the environment: programs started from the window manager
keep XMODIFIERS and their input method.

--- a/openbox/openbox.c
+++ b/openbox/openbox.c
@@ -191,7 +191,15 @@
     /* check for locale support */
     if (!XSupportsLocale())
         g_message(_("X server does not support locale."));
-    if (!XSetLocaleModifiers(""))
+    /* SDE: the window manager takes keys only for its bindings, menus and
+       prompts, so it never connects to the user's input method server
+       (XMODIFIERS=@im=ibus, fcitx...), only to the local one (Compose).
+       XIM calls wait for the server without a timeout: when IBus restarted,
+       the keymap change that followed made obt_keyboard_reload() wait in
+       XDestroyIC() for the old server forever, and no window could be
+       mapped, moved or focused any more. Programs started from the window
+       manager keep XMODIFIERS. */
+    if (!XSetLocaleModifiers("@im=none"))
         g_message(_("Cannot set locale modifiers for the X server."));
 
